#
# NOV26/HS
#
A few useful test programs for the Venix subsystem on TLVC.
The tiny* and small* programs are copies of the syscall_test.c binary using
the memory model/stack location indicated by the name. The high stack variants
have 2k stack, the low stack variants have 8k stacks (the linker default).

The syscalltst program is primariy useful for testing heap availability, but tests
a lot of other things too. Most useful if run with a filename as argument, 
like /linux. Also, even more useful if /etc/motd exists.

The crfeatefile.s program used to have a .c 'master' which was accidentally lost. 
The program simply prints binary 0 through 255 to the terminal/console (stdout).
